schema ProofFrontier
generation control-1
authority native-kernel
absorbs 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/proof_frontier.py
note The anti-amnesia spine. WorkGraph says what work remains; this says what knowledge is settled, and therefore what work is permitted. FPQ is the motivating case: a garbage generation at the top layer kept authorizing an encoder rewrite at the bottom.

truth_plane declared implemented measured proven
  note A comment claiming a property is declared. Only a witness makes it proven. A measured cosine is not a proof of behavioural equivalence, and a docstring claiming category isomorphism is not proof of one.

concept SolvedInvariant
  field invariant_id text identity
  field subject_resource text required
  field subject_profile text
  field subject_hashes list
  field layer text required
  field statement text required
  field truth_plane enum declared implemented measured proven
  field status enum cooled challenged invalidated
  field reheat_conditions list required-when-cooled
  invariant cooled-needs-a-way-back
    statement a cooled invariant must name what reheats it, or it is settled forever against reality
  invariant symptom-does-not-challenge
    statement only a signal matching a named reheat condition may move a cooled invariant to challenged

concept KnownNonCause
  field noncause_id text identity
  field hypothesis text required
  field subject_scope text required
  field experiment text required
  field witness_ref text
  field invalidation_conditions list
  note negative causal knowledge, often more valuable than another failure log. The FP16-passthrough and Q/K/V-bypass experiments each eliminated a hypothesis permanently.

concept ProofFrontier
  field subject_resource text required
  field subject_profile text
  ordered_layers source_model representation_abi reconstruction prepared_state transformer_math runtime_contract physical_execution semantic_behavior
  layer_status proven open blocked untested
  field first_open_layer derived
  field mutation_ceiling derived
  note the eight FPQ correctness layers, low to high; the frontier machinery is not FPQ-specific and applies to Bernstein adapters, Habitat, Frappe absorption equally

decision RegressionFence
  input target_layer observed_failure reheat_signal
  output allow deny
  rule deny-known-noncause
    statement if the failure matches a KnownNonCause for the subject, the target is not the cause
  rule deny-below-frontier
    statement a target layer below the first open layer is proven ground and off-limits
  rule reheat-only-on-named-signal
    statement a proven layer reopens only when a reheat signal satisfies a cooled invariant on it
  rule allow-at-or-above-frontier
    statement the open layer and above are the permitted work

law fix-fpq-is-a-prohibited-mission
  statement no mission may target model representation code on a bare "generation is garbage". It must name which profile, which artifact hash, which proof layer failed, which causes are already eliminated, and what evidence authorizes reheating that layer.
